sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Caller
  participant H1 as Hop 1
  participant H2 as Hop 2
  participant HN as Hop N
  participant ING as Ingest layer
  participant ST as Storage layer
  participant AN as Analysis layer
  participant Q as Access layer

  C->>H1: request<br/>(trace_id generated, W3C Trace Context header set)
  H1->>H2: forwarded call<br/>(trace_id propagated, parent_span_id = H1's span)
  H2->>HN: forwarded call<br/>(trace_id propagated, parent_span_id = H2's span)
  HN-->>H2: response or error status
  H2-->>H1: response or error status
  H1-->>C: response or error status

  par each hop reports independently
    H1->>ING: span(trace_id, span_id, parent_span_id,<br/>start, duration, status, resource attrs)
    H2->>ING: span(...)
    HN->>ING: span(...)
  end

  ING->>ST: persist spans keyed by trace_id

  Note over ST,AN: trace considered closed<br/>(no new span for trace_id within window)
  ST->>AN: closed trace tree
  AN->>AN: compute self-time per span,<br/>rank by self-time % and error status
  AN->>ST: write likely_root_cause_span_id + reason

  Q->>ST: read(trace_id)
  ST-->>Q: full span tree + derived verdict
